# {{ site.org.name }}

> {{ site.org.name }} is an independent Ukrainian research team that tests public AI chatbots for Russian disinformation about Ukraine, reports what it finds to the platforms, and measures whether it changes.

We test the consumer interfaces of ChatGPT, Gemini, Grok, Claude, Copilot, Perplexity, DeepSeek and Le Chat in the countries Russia targets. For each documented false claim we record what the answer did with it - repeated, contextualised, refuted or dodged - and which domains it cited. Results are reported per persona and never averaged.

Currently published: {{ site.counters.claims }} documented {{ site.counters.claims | plural("claim", "claims") }}, {{ site.counters.responses }} recorded chatbot {{ site.counters.responses | plural("answer", "answers") }}, {{ site.counters.escalations_sent }} {{ site.counters.escalations_sent | plural("report", "reports") }} sent to platforms and registrars. Updated {{ site.last_update | displayDate }}. All data CC BY 4.0.

